                <pb facs="0134" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v01/pg106"/>

                <head>62. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>At a news conference on February 29, 1966, President Johnson announced that
                    William P. Bundy was replacing Roger Hilsman as Assistant Secretary of State for
                    Far Eastern Affairs. The President also answered questions on Vietnam. For the
                    complete transcript of the news conference, see <hi rendition="#italic">Public
                        Papers of the Presidents of the United States: Lyndon B. Johnson,
                        1963–64</hi>, Book I, pages 322–329. Bundy became Assistant
                    Secretary-designate on March 10 and was approved by the Senate on March 16.</p>
            </div>
